Your enum underlying type is implementation-defined

If someone does:

jpeg_decode_scale_t scale = JPEG_SCALE_AUTO;

And internally you treat it like:

1 << scale   // 💀 boom (undefined behavior)
✅ Fix (safe approach)

Instead of -1, do:

JPEG_SCALE_AUTO = 255

OR:

JPEG_SCALE_AUTO = 0xFF
🧠 Why this is better
stays in unsigned domain
avoids accidental bit-shift bugs
safer in embedded contexts
